Insurance Management System

📌 Project Overview
The Insurance Management System is a database management project developed using MySQL to manage insurance customers, policies, premium payments, and claims efficiently.
🎯 Objectives
Organize customer and administrator information.
Manage insurance policies and categories.
Record policy purchases and premium payments.
Track insurance claims and their approval status.
Generate reports using SQL queries.

🛠️ Technologies Used
MySQL 8.0+
SQL
Relational Database Management System (RDBMS) concepts
✨ Key Features
Customer and administrator tables.
Multiple insurance policy categories.
Policy purchase and payment tracking.
Insurance claim management.
Customer feedback and notifications.
Stored procedure for premium calculation.
Trigger for claim-status notifications.
SQL queries using JOINs, subqueries, aggregate functions, and conditional statements.

🗄️ Database Tables
Admin
Customers
Policy Categories
Policies
Policy Purchases
Payments
Claims
Feedback
Notifications

🚀 How to Run
Install MySQL 8.0 or a compatible version.
Open MySQL Workbench.
Open the SQL source file.
Execute the script to create the database, tables, and sample records.
Run the example queries to explore the database.

📚 Learning Outcomes
This project demonstrates relational database design, primary and foreign keys, data integrity, joins, aggregate queries, stored procedures, triggers, and database operations.
